<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech SPT Telecom posts lower net profit.</title>
<headline>Czech SPT Telecom posts lower net profit.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech fixed line telephone monopoly SPT Telecom a.s. said on Wednesday it posted first half after-tax consolidated profits of 2.79 billion crowns versus 2.82 billion in the same period last year, according to international accounting standards (IAS).</p>
<p>SPT added that revenues rose to 18.9 billion crowns from 15.1 billion in the first half of 1996.  </p>
<p>Consolidated results, to international accounting standards, for period ending June 30, 1997 (in billions of crowns).</p>
<p> INCOME STATEMENT		   H1 1997    VS   H1 1996</p>
<p> Call revenues			11.473	    9.065</p>
<p> Other revenues			7.450	    6.032</p>
<p> Total revenues		     18.923	   15.097</p>
<p> Staff costs			   3.345	    2.873</p>
<p> Other costs			   6.599	    5.326</p>
<p> Total operating costs	     9.944	    8.199</p>
<p> EBITD				   8.979	    6.898</p>
<p> Depreciation			  3.971	    2.938</p>
<p> EBIT				    5.008	    3.960</p>
<p>Contributed services</p>
<p> from Telsource			0.424	    0.268</p>
<p> Interest expense		    0.823	    0.341</p>
<p> Interest income		    -0.389	   -0.485</p>
<p>Net foreign exchange</p>
<p> gains				  -0.439	   -0.643</p>
<p> Profit before tax		   4.589	    4.479</p>
<p> Income tax			    1.799	    1.661</p>
<p> Net profit after tax		2.790	    2.818</p>
<p> BALANCE SHEET			 H1 1997	VS  FULL YEAR '96</p>
<p> Fixed Assets			   88.091		    77.851</p>
<p> - tangible fixed assets	    67.091		    59.258</p>
<p> - construction in progress	 20.437		    18.122</p>
<p> - intangible fixed assets	   0.562		     0.470</p>
<p> - investments			   0.001		     0.001</p>
<p> Current Assets			 31.060		    28.316</p>
<p> - inventories			   2.361		     1.936</p>
<p> - receivables			   6.683		     7.162</p>
<p>- contributed services</p>
<p>   from TelSource			3.264		     2.953</p>
<p>- cash and cash</p>
<p>   equivalents			  18.752		    16.265</p>
<p> Total Assets			  119.151		   106.167</p>
<p> Total Equity			   82.024		    79.071</p>
<p> - share capital			32.209		    32.209</p>
<p> - reserves			     49.815		    46.862</p>
<p> Liabilities			    37.127		    27.096</p>
<p> - loans and overdrafts	     24.896		    16.025</p>
<p> - creditors			     6.933		     6.228</p>
<p>- finance lease</p>
<p>   obligations			   0.144		     0.117</p>
<p> - provisions			    5.154		     4.726</p>
<p>Total equity</p>
<p> and liabilities		     119.151		    106.167</p>
<p>NOTE : SPT Telecom, the most heavily capitalised share on the Prague bourse, said that all results are unaudited and presented under international accounting standards. It added that EuroTel Praha spol s.r.o., the 51 percent subsidiary of SPT active in the cellular market, has been consolidated on a line by line basis.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
